 "notes": "Scope: California districts 27-52 only (26 rows); the brief's per-state seat count (52) applies to the whole state, which is split across groups. All results are from the NBC Los Angeles results page (NBC News Decision Desk), updated 4 Nov 2026 10:54am, which labels a projected winner in every district 27-52; results are unofficial, not certified. CA-40: two sitting members (Ken Calvert beat Young Kim, K000397, who will not return); NBC projection, also reported by NBC Palm Springs 10 Nov; I did not find an AP call. CA-41: Linda Sánchez (previously the 38th) won the redrawn 41st over Mitch Clemmons; Calvert previously held the 41st and moved to the 40th. CA-34: sitting member Jimmy Gomez (G000585) lost to Angela Gonzales-Torres; AP also called it per news reports. CA-38: an AP item naming Linda Sánchez the 38th-district winner appeared in search, but it is undated and appears to be from 2024; NBC projects Hilda Solis over Pedro Casas for 2026. CA-48: AP called for Marni von Wilpert; Darrell Issa (I000056) retired. Backgrounds come from search summaries of campaign/news/BallotReady pages and were not individually opened."
